# internal source material — not for the public repo
Website Materials for Claude.docx

# local tooling
.claude/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Full-size photo and video originals.
#
# Everything on the site is optimised before it is committed — competition
# photos, slideshow slides and logos are all resized and re-encoded first, and
# a straight-off-the-camera file is typically 15–25 MB against roughly 200 KB
# for the version actually served. A handful of those going in by accident adds
# hundreds of megabytes to the repository that can never really be removed,
# because git keeps every version of every file forever.
#
# The rules below are deliberately broad: they match how cameras and phones
# name their exports, not where the files happen to sit, so an original is
# ignored wherever it is dropped. Optimised site assets are unaffected because
# they all use descriptive names (comp-2026-new-york.jpg, hl-04-helmet.jpg,
# sponsors/skf.svg) rather than camera numbering.
#
# If you have an original you genuinely need tracked, force it in with:
#   git add -f path/to/file.jpg
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# a scratch folder for drop-anything-here originals
_raw/
**/_raw/

# camera and phone export naming, anywhere in the tree
IMG_*
DSC[0-9]*
DSCF[0-9]*
DCIM/
EB[0-9]*
P[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]*
# browser "duplicate download" naming, e.g. y (3).jpg — the trailing * matters,
# without it the pattern would only match names that end at the closing paren
y (*

# formats that are never used to serve the site, only ever originals
*.HEIC
*.heic
*.HEIF
*.heif
*.CR2
*.NEF
*.ARW
*.DNG
*.RAF
*.ORF
*.MOV
*.mov
*.MP4.original

# loose media dropped in the project root
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.png
/*.webp
